To hide the scrollbar while maintaining scroll functionality, you need to target the specific browser's scrollbar styling properties. Since different browsers use different syntax, the most robust approach involves using **Webkit** properties (Chrome, Safari, Edge) alongside **standard** properties (Firefox).

Here is the complete CSS solution:

```css
.hide-scrollbar {
  /* For Chrome, Safari, Edge, and Opera (Webkit-based) */
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; /* Keeps momentum scrolling on iOS */
  overflow: auto; /* Or 'scroll' depending on your needs */
  overflow-y: auto; /* Hide vertical scrollbar */
  overflow-x: auto; /* Hide horizontal scrollbar (optional) */
}

/* Webkit-specific scrollbar hiding */
.hide-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar {
  display: none;
}

/* Firefox: Hide scrollbar using 'scrollbar-width' */
.hide-scrollbar {
  scrollbar-width: none; /* 'auto' shows it, 'none' hides it */
}
```

### How it works:
1.  **`overflow: auto`**: This ensures the element scrolls only when the content overflows, which is a prerequisite for the scrollbar to appear (and thus to be hidden).
2.  **`::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }`**: This targets the Webkit engine (Chrome, Safari, Edge) and completely removes the scrollbar element from the DOM rendering.
3.  **`scrollbar-width: none`**: This is the modern standard property used specifically for Firefox to suppress the scrollbar.

### Important Note on User Experience
While this hides the visual indicator, users won't immediately know the content is scrollable unless they use a mouse wheel, trackpad, or touch gesture. It is often good practice to add a subtle visual cue (like a shadow at the bottom or a slight gradient) to indicate there is more content below.

### Full Example
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  .container {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    overflow: auto; /* Enables scrolling */
    padding: 10px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  /* Hide scrollbar for Webkit browsers */
  .container::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Hide scrollbar for Firefox */
  .container {
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
  <p>This content is long. You can scroll normally, but the scrollbar is hidden.</p>
  <p>Line 2...</p>
  <p>Line 3...</p>
  <p>Line 4...</p>
  <p>Line 5...</p>
  <p>Line 6...</p>
  <p>Line 7...</p>
  <p>Line 8...</p>
  <p>Line 9...</p>
  <p>Line 10...</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```
